wit:
For all her toothless gums,—as Leigh himself
Would fain be a Christian still, for all his wit;
Pass that; you two may settle it, for me.

withdraws:
Break lashing me through hours of soulful dread;
But when the terror thins and, spent, withdraws,
Leaving me wondering awhile, I pause--

witnessed:
Have walked therein; and many more than these;
And witnessed the desire and the despair
Of souls that passed reluctantly and sicken for the air;

withering:
Until sere Autumn's fall;
But now that leaves are withering
How should one love at all?

wither:
I hear thy compassionate breath;
I wither, I fall, like the autumn-kissed leaf,
He gave me the roses of death, of death,

witnessing:
That Romney chose a wife, could write her name,
In witnessing he loved her.’
‘Loved!’ I cried;

witchcraft:
Without the accents. Read it? Not a word.
I saw at once the thing had witchcraft in’t
Whereof the reading calls up dangerous spirits;

withoutside:
We build our houses on the sand
Comely withoutside and within;
But when the winds and rains begin

withoutness:
Doth overflow his purpose with made heat,
And, like a clock, winds with withoutness willed
What should have been an inner instinct’s feat;
